-- The note on Hebrew language and expression (¶65-¶66): for teachers in
-- the project with a 50% external examination and a 50% school assessment,
-- 1 hour + 2% to each part.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b/p66
GIVEN `in the 50-50 project` IS A BOOLEAN, p IS AN `exam part`
GIVETH AN `allowance cell`
DECIDE `the Hebrew-expression part` `in the 50-50 project` p IS
    IF `in the 50-50 project`
    THEN `cell` 1 (2%)
    ELSE `the part of the allowance` (`cell` 2 (4%)) p

@ref akn:art_2__para_b/p76 akn:art_2__para_b/p77 akn:art_2__para_b/p78 akn:art_2__para_b/p79 akn:art_2__para_b/p80 akn:art_2__para_b/p81 akn:art_2__para_b/p82 akn:art_2__para_b/p83 akn:art_2__para_b/p84 akn:art_2__para_b/p85 akn:art_2__para_b/p86 akn:art_2__para_b/p87 akn:art_2__para_b/p88 akn:art_2__para_b/p89 akn:art_2__para_b/p90
`the electives with special rules` MEANS
    LIST `table row` `biology` 5 "questionnaire and laboratory" (`cell` 3.5 (2%)) (JUST (`cell` 3.5 (2%))) NOTHING,
         `table row` `biology` 5 "biotope or bio-research" (`cell` 1.5 0) NOTHING (JUST (`cell` 1.5 0)),
         `table row` `life sciences and agriculture` 5 "questionnaire" (`cell` 3.5 (2%)) (JUST (`cell` 3.5 (2%))) NOTHING,
         `table row` `life sciences and agriculture` 5 "biotope or bio-research" (`cell` 1.5 0) NOTHING (JUST (`cell` 1.5 0)),
         `table row` `environmental sciences` 5 "questionnaire" (`cell` 3.5 (2%)) (JUST (`cell` 3.5 (2%))) NOTHING,
         `table row` `environmental sciences` 5 "ecotope" (`cell` 1.5 0) NOTHING (JUST (`cell` 1.5 0)),
         `table row` `geography` 5 "questionnaire" (`cell` 3.5 (2%)) (JUST (`cell` 3.5 (2%))) NOTHING,
         `table row` `geography` 5 "geotope" (`cell` 1 0) NOTHING (JUST (`cell` 1 0)),
         `table row` `Land of Israel studies` 5 "questionnaire" (`cell` 3.5 (2%)) (JUST (`cell` 3.5 (2%))) NOTHING,
         `table row` `Land of Israel studies` 5 "geotope" (`cell` 1 0) NOTHING (JUST (`cell` 1 0))

@ref akn:art_2__para_b/p97 akn:art_2__para_b/p98
`the other electives` MEANS
    LIST `table row` `another elective subject` 5 "" (`cell` 3.5 (2%)) (JUST (`cell` 2.45 (1.4%))) (JUST (`cell` 1.05 (0.6%)))

`the table` MEANS
    concat (LIST `the compulsory subjects, first page`, `the compulsory subjects, second page`, `the electives with special rules`, `the other electives`)

-- Checks the table against section 1. A row that prints BOTH parts splits
-- its pre-reform allowance 70%-30%, in hours and in percent; a row that
-- prints ONE part carries the pre-reform allowance unchanged into it.
GIVEN a IS AN `allowance cell`, b IS AN `allowance cell`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the same cell` a b IF
    a's `cell weekly hours` EQUALS b's `cell weekly hours` AND a's `cell percent` EQUALS b's `cell percent`

GIVEN r IS A `table row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row agrees with section 1` r IF
    CONSIDER r's `external part`
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        CONSIDER r's `school part`
        WHEN JUST s THEN     `the same cell` e (`the part of the allowance` (r's `pre-reform`) `the external examination`)
                         AND `the same cell` s (`the part of the allowance` (r's `pre-reform`) `the school assessment`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the same cell` e (r's `pre-reform`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER r's `school part`
        WHEN JUST s THEN `the same cell` s (r's `pre-reform`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

#ASSERT all `the row agrees with section 1` `the table`
#ASSERT count `the table` EQUALS 36

-- F-2014-15_tashae_02-a: mathematics (3 units) and English print the
-- allowance per questionnaire, the school assessment taking the whole
-- allowance of the questionnaire it replaces. Summed over a subject-level,
-- the school part is then not 30%: English at 4 units has C (1 hour + 2%,
-- external) and D (1 hour + 2%, school), so half the allowance goes to the
-- school assessment where 1 ¶4 gives it 30%.
-- The reading adopted: the table's own rows govern the subjects it prints
-- per questionnaire, and `the allowance for the part` pays them as printed.
GIVEN s IS A `subject`, `units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `table row`
DECIDE `the rows for` s `units` IS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row subject` EQUALS s AND r's `row units` EQUALS `units`) `the table`

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF `table row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pre-reform hours of` rs IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `pre-reform`'s `cell weekly hours`) rs)

GIVEN r IS A `table row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the row's school-part hours` r IS
    CONSIDER r's `school part`
    WHEN JUST c  THEN c's `cell weekly hours`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF `table row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `school-part hours of` rs IS
    sum (map `the row's school-part hours` rs)

`English at 4 units` MEANS `the rows for` `English` 4

`the table gives English at 4 units half, not 30%, to the school part` MEANS
        `school-part hours of` `English at 4 units` EQUALS 1
    AND `pre-reform hours of` `English at 4 units` EQUALS 2
    AND NOT (`school-part hours of` `English at 4 units` EQUALS `the school share` TIMES `pre-reform hours of` `English at 4 units`)
#ASSERT `the table gives English at 4 units half, not 30%, to the school part`

-- Mathematics at 3 units: 0.5 of 2 hours (25%) and 2% of 6% (a third).
#ASSERT `school-part hours of` (`the rows for` `mathematics` 3) EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `pre-reform hours of` (`the rows for` `mathematics` 3) EQUALS 2

-- The allowance the table gives a teacher for one row and one part, by
-- the class size.
@export default The matriculation preparation allowance a teacher is paid for one row of the table of owners' circular 2014-15/2, for one part of the examination and a class of a given size
GIVEN r IS A `table row` @desc the row of the table (subject, units, component)
      p IS AN `exam part` @desc the external examination or the school assessment
      `pupils` IS A NUMBER @desc the number of pupils the teacher presents
GIVETH AN `allowance cell`
DECIDE `the allowance for the part` r p `pupils` IS
    LET `printed` MEANS
            CONSIDER p
            WHEN `the external examination` THEN r's `external part`
            WHEN `the school assessment`    THEN r's `school part`
    IN CONSIDER `printed`
       WHEN JUST c  THEN `cell` (c's `cell weekly hours` TIMES `the share for the class size` `pupils`) (c's `cell percent` TIMES `the share for the class size` `pupils`)
       WHEN NOTHING THEN `cell` 0 0

-- Examples: history, 2 units, a class of 8 (50%).
`the history row` MEANS `table row` `history` 2 "" (`cell` 1.5 (2%)) (JUST (`cell` 1.05 (1.4%))) (JUST (`cell` 0.45 (0.6%)))

#ASSERT `the same cell` (`the allowance for the part` `the history row` `the external examination` 8) (`cell` 0.525 (0.7%))
#ASSERT `the same cell` (`the allowance for the part` `the history row` `the school assessment` 30) (`cell` 0.45 (0.6%))
#ASSERT `the share for the class size` 5 EQUALS 25%
#ASSERT `the share for the class size` 9 EQUALS 50%
#ASSERT NOT `the examination has a school assessment` `mathematics` 5 2014
#ASSERT `the examination has a school assessment` `history` 2 2014
#ASSERT NOT `the assessment earns a preparation allowance` `an internal assessment` FALSE
#ASSERT `the same cell` (`the Hebrew-expression part` TRUE `the school assessment`) (`cell` 1 (2%))
#ASSERT `the same cell` (`the Hebrew-expression part` FALSE `the school assessment`) (`cell` 0.6 (1.2%))

#TRACE `the external part paid in its year` (`cell` 1.5 (2%)) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the external part` (`cell` 1.05 (1.4%)) AT 10
